miniBox - a determinism sandbox derived from the waterbox subsystem of BizHawk
(https://github.com/TASEmulators/BizHawk).

miniBox combines several upstream projects, each under its own permissive
license, plus new work authored for miniBox. A complete, component-by-component
inventory of authorship and licenses is in docs/ATTRIBUTION.md. In summary:

- The waterbox itself - the runtime (host), emulibc, libco's amd64 backend, the
  libcxx build scripts, linkscript, and build machinery - is the BizHawk team's
  MIT-licensed work.
- toolchain/musl (git submodule) is a fork of musl libc, Copyright (c) 2005-2020
  Rich Felker and contributors, MIT (see that submodule's COPYRIGHT file).
- libco is by byuu (Near), released into the public domain.
- extern/vulkan-headers is the Khronos Group's Vulkan headers and registry,
  Apache-2.0 OR MIT, unmodified (see its LICENSE.md).
- The LLVM libraries built by toolchain/libcxx (libc++, libc++abi, libunwind,
  compiler-rt) are the LLVM contributors' work, Apache-2.0 with the LLVM
  exception; they are fetched and built, not vendored here.
- The Rust runtime's crate dependencies (MIT/Apache-2.0) are fetched at build
  time, not vendored here.

All of the above are mutually compatible. miniBox's own new work, and the
combined distribution, are provided under the MIT License, whose text is in
LICENSE.
